{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/81007-making-a-table-top-rpg","id":81007,"title":"Making a Table Top RPG.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-27T06:54:36-08:00","id":81007,"title":"Making a Table Top RPG.","content":"So I have two in the works, One is in the beta phase/editing. The other is still in concept in design because I am going all out on the Character Creation (no two people should ever have the same character unless intentional.) in how many options in Character building there are so far. So what is it that YOU look for in an rpg? I would like to hear the Gamers perspective. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2392-happyevilgaming","name":"HappyEvilGaming","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2392_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T07:40:11-08:00","id":81026,"title":"","content":"Answer: It depends on the game.<br /> <br /> What I look for in a Call of Cthulhu game is far and away from what I look for in say Exalted, World of Darkness or Paranoia type game. Broadly, character creation should be simple and fairly fast, the mechanics of the game shouldn't get in the way of playing the game, and the Setting and mechanics both should work towards maintaining the tone of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> I will however add that your comment that you're piling in vast numbers of options into the game you're in the early stages of designing makes me wary, since nigh-unlimited options means large amounts of time picking and choosing in character creation, and thus with the very introduction have made me less inclined to have any interest in it no matter the actual material.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T08:09:33-08:00","id":81035,"title":"","content":"Simple dice. I can deal with D10 and D6, but more than that (D4 through D20) turns me off. Not everyone has enough of those to share about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T08:52:52-08:00","id":81075,"title":"","content":"I have a rule about games - and it is kind of a tricky one. A game must have one of the following statements be true for me to enjoy it (based on historical evidence):<br /> <br /> A) Creating a full set of new characters and diving into actually playing the game takes no more than 30 minutes, even if none of the players were expecting to be playing a game that day (partial list of examples: D&amp;D before 3rd edition, all of the World of Darkness games, Dungeon Crawl Classics)<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> B) The character creation process is somewhat lengthy, but every added minute of character creation is accompanied by choices which are genuinely meaningful in game-play, and every &quot;my character is different because...&quot; has actual impact on game-play (complete list of examples: Shadowrun, HackMaster)<br /> <br /> In both cases, however, game-play must flow smoothly at a fast pace so that a single 4 hour session feels like tons of progress could be made.<br /> <br /> There is also a clause about how easy it is to lose a character, which must be relative to how long making a new character takes (shorter character creation = okay for less-forgiving game-play; longer character creation = can't actually lose a character without specifically choosing to do so, usually by way of electing not to spend character resources specifically designed to let you keep a character as long as you want to)<br /> <br /> And, a random bit of advice from one fledgling designer to another: Don't be different just to be different - make sure anything you are doing differently from another game has a genuine purpose and significantly impacts game-play (example: don't base your game around Attribute + Skill pools of d8 just because d6 and d10 are already in use by some other game - but certainly do so if the way you want the game-math to work out is easier to achieve because of d8s)<br /> <br /> Reinventing the wheel has basically never done anyone any good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}